Go to your Chrome browser and search KALI LINUX.
Click on the first option which is GET KALI.
Under it you'll see INSTALLER IMAGES & VIRTUAL MACHINES.
Go for VIRTUAL MACHINES PLATFORM.
Under virtual machines,scroll down and look for VIRTUAL BOX as recommendation
Click the download, it will take a while to download probably 3.6GB
Inside your chrome browser seaerch for 7-zip file manager and download it based on your system type.
Go to your DOWNLOADS to install the 7-zip by simply right clicking on it.
Once installed still in your downloads folder right click on KALI linux.
Look for 7-ZIP if you can't find it go to "SHOW MORE OPTIONS"
Inside 7-ZIP choose EXTRACT ALL,it will extract kali linux then you will see two files virtual disk image and vitual machine definition file.
GO to your virtualbox and click IMPORT then locate your kali linux in your downloads and click OPEN.
Once imported you'll see it settings in virtualbox.
When starting up your Kali linux, the USERNAME & PASSWORD is Kali in lowercase.
FOR CONFIGURATION OF VIRTUAL MACHINE
Click on settings and ensure you're inside EXPERT MODE
Click FEATURES and make sure you drag and drop to BIDIRECTIONAL.it allows yout to share links and files between your host which is windows and virtual machine.
Go to your network and check your network adapter.chosose NAT network to share your internet with the virtual machine.
If you want kali to have it own IP address on your network then select BRIDGE ADAPTER,this allows your wifi to assign a separate IP to your kali linux.
Every other settings just leave it at DEFAULT and start your kali linux.
